  "requirements": "* Differentiate the tanh activation using the cached hidden state\n* Compute input and previous-state gradients with transposed weight matrices\n* Compute both weight gradients as outer products\n* Return exactly dx_t, dh_prev, dW, dU, and db in a dictionary",
  "theory": "## What Is RNN Step Backward (Vanilla RNN)?\n\nIn scientific array computing with NumPy, vectorized tensor operations apply mathematical transformations across entire arrays without Python loop overhead.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{z}_t=W\\mathbf{x}_t+U\\mathbf{h}_{t-1}+\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\n---\n\n## Mathematical Formulation & Theoretical Mechanics\n\nSupervised and unsupervised learning algorithms minimize empirical risk over a hypothesis space $\\mathcal{H}$ while regularizing model capacity to balance bias and variance on unseen test distributions.\n\nThe full mathematical structure is governed by the coupled relations:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{h}_t=\\tanh(\\mathbf{z}_t)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{d z}=\\mathbf{d h}\\odot(1-\\mathbf{h}_t^2)\n$$\n\n---\n\n## Key Properties & Conceptual Intuition\n\n- **Inductive Bias & Capacity Control:** Regularization penalties ($L_1$, $L_2$, pruning, or ensemble averaging) constrain effective hypothesis complexity and prevent overfitting to training noise.\n- **Decision Boundary Geometry:** Linear models partition feature space with hyperplanes, distance-based methods induce Voronoi tessellations, and tree ensembles form axis-aligned orthotopes.\n- **Related Topics in This Track:** **Backpropagation Through Time**, **RNN Cell**, **Forward Through Sequence**.\n\n---\n\n## Numerical Stability & Boundary Behavior\n\n- **Conditioning & Degenerate Regimes:** When denominators, norms, or variances approach zero on constant or collinear inputs, additive regularization ($\\varepsilon > 0$) or limiting analytical values prevent division-by-zero instabilities.\n- **Scale & Precision Invariance:** Formulating updates via centered shifts (such as log-sum-exp shifting for exponentials or Welford-style centering for moments) avoids catastrophic cancellation and floating-point overflow.\n\n---\n\n## Computational Complexity\n\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N \\cdot d)$ (or $\\mathcal{O}(N \\cdot M \\cdot d)$ for matrix-matrix products) to evaluate the linear projections and inner products.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N \\cdot d)$ to store the projected representations and output array.",
