  "solution": "### \ud83d\udca1 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### \ud83d\udcbb Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef rnn_step_backward(dh: list, cache: list) -> dict:\n    x_t, h_prev, h_t, Wx, Wh, b = cache\n    dh_arr = np.array(dh, dtype=float)\n    h_t_arr = np.array(h_t, dtype=float)\n    x_t_arr = np.array(x_t, dtype=float)\n    h_prev_arr = np.array(h_prev, dtype=float)\n    Wx_arr = np.array(Wx, dtype=float)\n    Wh_arr = np.array(Wh, dtype=float)\n    dtanh = dh_arr * (1.0 - h_t_arr ** 2)\n    dx_t = dtanh @ Wx_arr\n    dh_prev = dtanh @ Wh_arr\n    dW = np.outer(dtanh, x_t_arr)\n    dU = np.outer(dtanh, h_prev_arr)\n    db = dtanh\n    return {'dx_t': np.round(dx_t, 6).tolist(), 'dh_prev': np.round(dh_prev, 6).tolist(), 'dW': np.round(dW, 6).tolist(), 'dU': np.round(dU, 6).tolist(), 'db': np.round(db, 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### \u23f1\ufe0f Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
